  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "items": [
        "Each row is one ownership lane and each column is one runtime; the text in a cell is the actual owner for that lane on that runtime.",
        "All four lanes differ per runtime, which is why switching runtimes is not switching a model backend — it replaces the whole execution and persistence chain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Only cancel is shared",
      "items": [
        "A capability is not a feature flag; it is part of the implementation and cannot be enabled by configuration.",
        "dsh-native has session events and persistence, harness has durable receipts and child tasks, codex has replay and build binding — the only capability all three share is cancel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why native-engine gets its own column",
      "items": [
        "It can be selected by routing but is not in the official value list the creation form offers, so it has no comparable capabilities next to the other three.",
        "Until its resource tools move onto the protocol, the creation form, portable bundles and deployments will not offer it."
      ]
    }
  ]
